<h2>Start with the rule set</h2><p>Challenge accounts introduce constraints beyond the trade idea itself. Keep the program’s daily loss calculation, overall loss limit and reset schedule visible before every session.</p><h2>Track the right measure</h2><p>Check whether the provider uses equity or balance and whether open profit and loss affects a limit. A tool’s settings must match the actual program; a default setting is not confirmation that an account remains compliant.</p><h2>Make the provider the reference</h2><p>Review the provider’s account dashboard and terms whenever there is uncertainty. Monitoring tools can support a routine, but they cannot guarantee that a breach will be prevented.</p><p>Looking for the dedicated FYNX evaluation platform? Visit <a href="https://fynxfunded.com">FYNX Funded</a> for current options and requirements.</p>